course: dictionary
lesson: 10991
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word wart can mean a lump on your skin, or any small lump on a plant or animal. «A warthog's warts are thick bumpy pads that protect its face in fights.» The clues are warthog and face in fights, so here a wart is a bumpy pad on an animal.
explain: Always ask: what is the subject of the sentence? A wart on a hand is a human skin problem, and a wart on a warthog is an animal feature. «Warts are caused by a human virus, so toads can't give you warts.» Here the word human tells you the warts are on people.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If «a small, hard lump» still makes sense, you have probably got it right. If it does not, read the words around it again.
fact: A wart is a small, hard, rough lump that grows on the skin.
fact: Warts are caused by a virus, and they often grow on hands or feet.
fact: A wart can also be any small lump on a plant or animal's skin.
fact: Toads cannot give you warts, but wash your hands after touching one, because some toads have skin that irritates.
fact: «Warts and all» means including all the bad parts, not just the good ones.
exercise: «Warts are caused by a virus, so toads can't give you warts.» What causes warts? | Toads | Cold weather | *A virus | Rain
exercise: «A warthog's warts are thick bumpy pads that protect its face in fights.» What are the warts on a warthog? | Long, sharp teeth | Spots that wash off | *Thick bumpy pads that protect its face | Soft, smooth feathers
exercise: «A verruca is a wart on the foot.» Where does a verruca grow? | *On the foot | In the mouth | On the head | On the hands
test: «She told him the film was good, warts and all.» What does warts and all mean here? | Warm and dry | Only the good parts | Hidden under a blanket | *Including all the bad parts too
test: Why should you not pick a wart? | It will start to glow | It makes you taller | *It can spread by touch | It turns into a toad
exam: Can toads give you warts? | Yes, always, in every country | Only in fairy tales | *No, warts are caused by a virus, not by toads | Yes, if you hold one
